  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 134 PM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nOn Friday night and Saturday, a broad shortwave will briefly impinge \non the ridge, driving very modest cyclogenesis over the Northern \nPlains. As a result, much of the deterministic guidance depicts a \nweak warm front extending to the southeast of the shortwave and into \nthe Mid-Mississippi Valley. This will support widespread cloud \ncoverage on Saturday and perhaps some light precipitation closer\nto the shortwave. In fact, LREF probabilities of at least 0.01\"\nof QPF exceed 50% in northeastern MO and west-central IL on \nSaturday afternoon. Given the weak forcing, I do not expect any \nof this precipitation to be impactful, but it should help pull \ntemperatures back down a bit. \n\nRidging will take hold again on Sunday and into Monday ahead of a \nsharp shortwave that's expected to move through the central CONUS \nsometime on Tuesday or Wednesday. This will be our next chance for \nwidespread precipitation across the region, with LREF 24 hour \nprobabilities of > 0.01\" around 100% and > 0.25\" over 50%.",
